Third-party sources and attribution
-----------------------------------

The files contain only (1) figures calculated by World Money Roadmap,
(2) U.S. government works, and (3) calendar dates taken from official
public notices. No third-party market price series is included.

data/fed-rate-history.csv
  Source: Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System,
  Open Market Operations table,
  https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/openmarket.htm
  Status: public domain (https://www.federalreserve.gov/disclaimer.htm).

data/us-financials-sec.csv
  Source: U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, EDGAR XBRL
  companyfacts API (10-Q and 10-K filings),
  https://www.sec.gov/edgar/sec-api-documentation
  Status: U.S. government work, public domain. Credit: "Source: U.S. SEC".

data/market-dates.csv
  Dates compiled from official public notices; the source_url column of
  each row links to its notice:
  - NYSE Group holiday and early-close announcement (ICE investor relations)
  - Korea Astronomy and Space Science Institute, calendar of official
    public holidays (Korean market holidays not yet announced by the Korea
    Exchange are marked "expected")
  - A Korean broker's guide page to the KOSPI 200 expiration rule
    (second Thursday of the month)
  - Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, FOMC meeting calendar
    (public domain)
  - U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics release schedules for the Consumer
    Price Index and the Employment Situation (public domain,
    https://www.bls.gov/developers/termsOfService.htm)
  - Cboe Global Markets, monthly options expiration rule
  - State Street Global Advisors, SPDR ETF distribution schedule
    (SPY, DIA, MDY)
  Dates are facts; no text, tables or logos from these sources are copied.
  NYSE, ICE, Korea Exchange, KOSPI, Cboe, SPDR and State Street are trademarks of their
  respective owners and are named only to identify the source.

data/trading-days.csv
  Calculated by World Money Roadmap from the NYSE holiday calendar and
  Korean market holidays (same sources as market-dates.csv).

data/ai-lab-nav.csv, data/ai-lab-metrics.csv
  Calculated by World Money Roadmap from paper (hypothetical) accounts in
  the site's AI investing experiment. No real money and no personal
  holdings. Only the benchmark's period return appears; no benchmark price
  series is included.

